3. **Add a safety check**: if after 150 steps the car is still far left (`p < -0.3`) force a “hard left” (`a = 0`) for a few steps to guarantee enough momentum before giving up on the episode. This can be added as an optional fallback rule.

With these changes the agent should consistently reach the top of the right hill well before the 200‑step limit, yielding an average return close to **‑15 to ‑20** (instead of the current **‑151**). This is the most effective deterministic strategy we have derived from the observed data.
