| Condition | Reasoning |
|-----------|-----------|
| `p >= 0.5` | Episode is already finished – no need to waste a step. |
| `0.45 ≤ p < 0.5` | We are within a few centimeters of the top; a neutral action prevents unnecessary acceleration that could push us back down. |
| `v > 0 ∧ p > -0.2` | The car has already crossed the valley bottom and is moving uphill; continue accelerating right to reach the summit quickly. |
| `v < 0 ∧ p < -0.2` | Still on the left slope and moving left; accelerating left increases the magnitude of the speed, which later translates into a stronger rightward push. |
| `p < -0.55` | Deep in the left valley – the only way out is to keep accelerating left until enough kinetic energy is built. |
| `v > 0` (center region) | Positive velocity on the flat part means we have already turned; push right. |
| `v < 0` (center region) | Negative velocity on the flat part means we are still sliding left; keep pushing left. |
| `else` | Catch‑all – do nothing. |

