| Very large negative velocities (`v < –0.1`) | Keep `action = 0` even if `p > –0.55` | The car is already moving fast left; braking would waste momentum. The rule above already does this because `velocity > 0` is false, so we fall into the *else* branch → `action = 2`. If we want to be more aggressive we could add: `ELIF velocity < –0.1 THEN action = 0`. |

