| Assumption | Reality |
|------------|---------|
| **“If velocity is already > 0, I can stop accelerating soon.”** | True **only** when the car is already high enough on the right slope (≈ ≥ 0.4). Otherwise it will coast back. |
| **“A hard left‑thrust at any negative velocity will always help.”** | Not true – if the car is still on the right side of the valley a left thrust pushes it *down* the slope and wastes steps. |
