**Bottom line:**  
The best performing policy is the one that **(i)** lets the car *build momentum on the left side* with a brief left‑push, **(ii)** then *accelerates right aggressively* while the velocity is still modest, and **(iii)** *coasts* once the velocity is safely above a “coast‑threshold”.  Anything that keeps the engine on full thrust when the car already has enough speed simply burns extra steps.

