| **Valley centre** | Coasts once velocity > 0.06 (enough kinetic energy). Otherwise continues to accelerate right. | Keeps the engine on only when it actually adds speed, reducing unnecessary –1 penalties. |
| **Right‑hill approach** | A tighter coast‑threshold (0.07) – slightly higher than in the best‑so‑far policy (0.07 vs 0.06) – and a small “boost‑if‑slow” clause (velocity > 0.02 → right). | Guarantees that the car does not stall near the goal; the tiny boost helps it cross the 0.5 mark without overshooting and then stopping. |
| **Goal** | As soon as `position >= 0.5` the policy stops accelerating (action = 1). | No extra thrust after the goal, so the episode ends at the earliest possible timestep. |

The thresholds (‑0.55, ‑0.2, 0.4, 0.07, ‑0.04, 0.02) were chosen by looking at the trajectories you posted:

