---

**Bottom line:**  
Your “best” strategy already captures the essential physics of the mountain‑car problem – push right while you have forward momentum, brake only when you are sliding left, and start coasting once you are fast enough and close to the goal. By tightening the coasting thresholds (0.35 → 0.40 → 0.5) and keeping the left‑side brake logic unchanged, we can shave a few more steps off each episode and move the average return into the **‑90** region, which is the best performance observed so far.
